## 3. Modular Background / Scene-Dressing System

### 3.1 Background manifest

```jsonc
{
  "id": "school_hallway",
  "type": "parallax-layered",        // "parallax-layered" | "tilemap" | "static"
  "layers": [
    { "name": "sky",     "source": "layers/sky.png",     "scroll_factor": 0.1, "depth": -30 },
    { "name": "far",     "source": "layers/far.png",      "scroll_factor": 0.4, "depth": -20 },
    { "name": "near",    "source": "layers/near.png",     "scroll_factor": 0.8, "depth": -10 }
  ],
  "tilemap": {
    "format": "tiled-json",
    "source": "tiles/hallway.json",
    "collision_layer": "collision"
  },
  "ambient_tint": "#1a1a1a",
  "ambient_audio": "audio/amb_hallway.ogg"
}
```

Requirements:

- A **`BackgroundLoader`** that supports three interchangeable rendering
  strategies (parallax layer stack, Tiled tilemap with collision, or a flat
  static image) selected purely by the manifest's `type` field — the calling
  scene code should call one function, `BackgroundLoader.build(sceneKey,
  backgroundId)`, and get back a handle exposing `.destroy()`,
  `.getCollisionLayer()`, and `.setAmbientTint(color)` regardless of which
  strategy was used underneath.
- Parallax scroll factors must work with Phaser's camera automatically as the
  player/camera moves — no manual per-frame scroll math in gameplay code.
- Swapping a background (e.g., moving to a new "level/day" in the loop) must
  be a single call: `BackgroundLoader.swap(newBackgroundId)`, cleanly
  destroying the old layers/tilemap and building the new one, with an
  optional transition hook (fade, wipe) supplied by the Screen/Mode system
  (section 4).
- Background manifests are discovered the same way sprite manifests are — by
  the `AssetRegistry` scanning `/graphics/backgrounds/*/manifest.json` — so
  adding a new background never requires an engine code change.

